    "problem_statement": "SVG QR code generation fails with TypeError on coordinate operations\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes using the SVG image factory, the code fails with a TypeError related to unsupported operand types. This affects all SVG-based QR code generation.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image import svg\nimport io\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data(\"test data\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=svg.SvgImage)\nimg.save(io.BytesIO())\n```\n\nThis will raise a TypeError when trying to save the SVG image.\n\nThe same issue occurs with other SVG factories:\n\n```python\n# Also fails\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=svg.SvgFragmentImage)\nimg.save(io.BytesIO())\n```\n\nAnd when using the command line interface:\n\n```bash\nqr \"test data\" --factory svg\n```"
  }
